<!DOCTYPE html>
<html>
<head>
    <title>Strong vs Bold Example</title>
</head>
<body>
    <h1>Strong vs Bold</h1>
    <p>
        Warning message with <b>bold styling only</b> — it looks bold, 
        but it's just for visual emphasis.
    </p>
    <p>
        Warning message with <strong>critical importance</strong> — 
        it not only looks bold, but screen readers will emphasize it for users 
        who rely on accessibility tools.
    </p>
    <h2>Practical Use Case:</h2>
    <p>
        <b>Menu item:</b> Chocolate Cake  
        <strong>Allergy Alert:</strong> Contains nuts
    </p>
</body>
</html>
